WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:04.240
Gather round, boys, girls, and&nbsp;
those who are young at heart!&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:09.280
We've talked a lot before about the wacky,&nbsp;
occasionally wonderful but always weird creations&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:15.280
of the mysterious toymaker Dr. Wondertainment,&nbsp;
and today we're going to do it again. It's time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:21.200
to crack open the SCP Foundation's toy&nbsp;
chest and see what we can find inside!&nbsp;

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:25.520
Dr. Wondertainment's inventions have been&nbsp;
attracting the attention of the Foundation for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:31.760
quite some time, and with good reason! Whoever&nbsp;
or whatever the whimsical, talented Dr. is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:36.400
there's no one else out there producing quite&nbsp;
as many anomaly objects and marketing them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:40.960
to children as playthings. These aren't the&nbsp;
toys you'll find in your neighborhood store&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:47.600
or on someone's Amazon wishlist. There's SCP-445,&nbsp;
the Super Paper that comes alive in the form of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:55.520
whatever you fold it into! SCP-1508, or Mikey the&nbsp;
Chore Buddy, a living cardboard robot designed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.520 --> 00:01:00.960
to help kids with their chores! There are the&nbsp;
adorable-yet-destructive fire-breathing Dragon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:09.680
Snails, or SCP-111, or SCP-958, General Beep, who&nbsp;
teaches kids about military history and combat,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:14.960
and helps them build real working toy weapons!
I could keep taking us through the proverbial&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:20.640
toy factory, but we'd be here all day. Maybe&nbsp;
Dr. Wondertainment's most anomalous trait&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:25.120
is how productive he manages to be!&nbsp;
I can barely send a single email&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:30.400
without three cups of coffee! But anyway...
One of the most well-known Dr. Wondertainment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:34.960
creations is the Little Misters line,&nbsp;
a series of humanoid playmates with a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:40.160
variety of different traits. We've covered the&nbsp;
Little Misters here on SCP Explained before,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:46.960
but let's do a quick refresh just in case.
There's Mr. Chameleon, Mr. Headless, Mr. Laugh,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:55.280
Mr. Forgetful, Mr. Shapey, Mr. Soap, Mr. Hungry,&nbsp;
Mr. Brass, Mr. Hot, Mr. Life and Mr. Death,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.280 --> 00:02:05.920
Mr. Fish, Mr. Moon, Mr. Redd, Mr. Money, Mr. Lost,&nbsp;
Mr. Lie, Mr. Mad, Mr. Scary, and Mr. Stripes. Each&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:11.200
of these little misters, from the top hat-wearing&nbsp;
fish to the man who can't remember a thing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:17.120
they're each special in their own way. But wait&nbsp;
a minute… Looking at them all lined up like that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:21.840
I can't help but feel like I'm missing&nbsp;
something. It seems like a bit of a boy's club,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:27.440
right? And why let boys have all the fun?
Well, it seems like Dr. Wondertainment thought&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:34.960
the very same thing, because he made a Little&nbsp;
Mister just for the girls! Enter Ms. Sweetie, the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:41.280
sweetest, pinkest gal around! At first glance, you&nbsp;
might mistake Ms. Sweetie for an ordinary woman,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:46.640
aside from her naturally pink hair and&nbsp;
eyes. No wig or contact lenses here! But,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:52.880
like the rest of her fellow Misters, Ms. Sweetie&nbsp;
has more to her than meets the eye. So what lies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.880 --> 00:02:58.320
beneath that candy-coated, sugary exterior?
To crack open that hard candy shell and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.320 --> 00:03:03.360
get at the truth inside, we'll have to look&nbsp;
a few years back, to when Ms. Sweetie first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:08.480
caught the attention of the Foundation!
It all started in a small, unassuming town&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.480 --> 00:03:12.640
tucked away in a valley, flanked on&nbsp;
either side by mountains and thick&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.640 --> 00:03:18.800
forests. It was a peaceful place, if a bit boring.&nbsp;
The worst thing anyone could remember happening in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:25.200
years was a cheating scandal at the yearly pie&nbsp;
bake-off. Then, ten-year-old Nina went missing.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:29.040
Her family was terrified, they called the&nbsp;
police right away, but the authorities&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:33.360
insisted that it looked like a classic case&nbsp;
of a little girl running away from home.&nbsp;

00:03:33.360 --> 00:03:38.320
After all, she'd taken her backpack, her&nbsp;
favorite toys, some sandwiches and bottles&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:43.600
of water from the fridge. She would come back&nbsp;
home soon, probably later that day, and everyone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.600 --> 00:03:49.680
would be able to laugh about this by tomorrow.
But tomorrow came, and Nina still didn't return&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.680 --> 00:03:56.000
home. People began to whisper, the way folks in&nbsp;
small towns always talk behind each others' backs.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.000 --> 00:04:02.640
Was there trouble at home? Nina had seemed like&nbsp;
such a happy girl, so outgoing, leading her troupe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:08.960
in girl scout cookie sales every year and singing&nbsp;
solos in the school choir. Something must have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:08.960 --> 00:04:15.840
been wrong, though. Otherwise, where did she go?
Then, others began to disappear. Tommy Bowers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.840 --> 00:04:21.280
was last spotted walking home from school. He fell&nbsp;
behind his friends, stopping to tie his shoe. When&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.280 --> 00:04:26.720
they noticed he was no longer with them, and went&nbsp;
back, he was gone. Then, Mikey Paulson vanished on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.720 --> 00:04:32.160
a camping trip in the nearby forest. His father&nbsp;
left him alone for a second in broad daylight,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:36.480
just to gather some firewood for later that&nbsp;
evening, and when he called out to his son for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.480 --> 00:04:42.080
help carrying it, there was no reply. One boy was&nbsp;
catching toads in the creek behind his house when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.080 --> 00:04:47.680
he disappeared. Another was seemingly snatched&nbsp;
while walking his dog. The dog, unharmed, ran&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:53.760
back home on her own, dragging her leash behind&nbsp;
her as she went. It had started with Nina, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.760 --> 00:04:59.680
now no one could be certain if it would stop. The&nbsp;
townspeople began to panic, wondering who would be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.680 --> 00:05:05.360
next? Who was taking their children? And why?
As it always does in small communities in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.360 --> 00:05:11.440
grip of terror, suspicion began to grow. Neighbors&nbsp;
turned on each other, pointing fingers at anyone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.440 --> 00:05:17.040
who seemed the least bit suspicious. Local police&nbsp;
were baffled by the sudden slew of apparent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:17.040 --> 00:05:22.400
kidnappings. Sure, they had a few potential&nbsp;
suspects, an elderly woman that the local&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.400 --> 00:05:28.400
kids claimed was a witch, a school groundskeeper&nbsp;
that just had a generally weird vibe about him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.400 --> 00:05:34.080
but none of the leads ever went anywhere. There&nbsp;
was no evidence found at any of the scenes.&nbsp;

00:05:34.080 --> 00:05:39.600
Where there were footprints, there was only one&nbsp;
set: the child's, leading off into the woods&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.600 --> 00:05:45.280
until they could no longer be tracked. Tensions&nbsp;
were mounting, and no one could trust anyone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:50.560
anymore. In a town where people had always left&nbsp;
their doors unlocked, people were boarding up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.560 --> 00:05:55.280
their windows, pulling their children out of&nbsp;
school, and keeping them home at all hours&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.280 --> 00:06:00.880
of the day. If they didn't, after all,&nbsp;
their child could be the next to vanish.&nbsp;

00:06:00.880 --> 00:06:05.040
After a week of nail-biting tension and&nbsp;
looking for threats around every corner,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.040 --> 00:06:12.240
the town was treated to a shocking surprise. Nina&nbsp;
came home. Casual as you please, her parents saw&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.240 --> 00:06:17.840
her come skipping down the driveway, a little&nbsp;
dirty and clearly exhausted, but cheerful. They&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:17.840 --> 00:06:22.240
embraced her, weeping, and she hugged them&nbsp;
tight, asking them to please stop crying.&nbsp;

00:06:22.240 --> 00:06:26.720
"We didn't know where you were!" Her mother&nbsp;
sobbed. "Didn't know if you were okay, or..."

00:06:26.720 --> 00:06:31.680
"I'm fine!" Nina insisted.
"They let you go?" Her father asked.&nbsp;

00:06:31.680 --> 00:06:36.640
"What? I just got hungry, and I missed&nbsp;
you, so I came back." Nina explained.&nbsp;

00:06:36.640 --> 00:06:42.240
"Who took you?" Her mother asked.
"No one took me, I was visiting my friend." Nina&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.240 --> 00:06:48.160
laughed. Her parents stared at her in shock.
"What...friend?" Her father stammered.&nbsp;

00:06:48.160 --> 00:06:52.480
"The pink lady in the woods," Nina said&nbsp;
simply, and then she rushed inside to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:52.480 --> 00:06:57.680
grab a snack and say hello to the family cat.
Police came by the house to speak with Nina, and,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:57.680 --> 00:07:01.840
after talking in circles about her friend in the&nbsp;
woods, and refusing to say that she was kidnapped,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:08.240
she agreed to show the officers where this "lady&nbsp;
in the woods" was. Other than her location,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.240 --> 00:07:14.240
all they could get out of Nina was that the lady&nbsp;
was "pink," she could "do magic," and she had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.240 --> 00:07:19.440
"lots of friends." They had no way to know for&nbsp;
certain, but they hoped that this mysterious&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:19.440 --> 00:07:25.120
woman would lead them to the missing boys. So,&nbsp;
that same day, a team of police officers, none&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:25.120 --> 00:07:30.480
of whom had ever seen more action than a parking&nbsp;
ticket or a teenage vandal spray painting a wall,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:30.480 --> 00:07:35.280
set out to recover the kidnapped&nbsp;
children from the lady in the woods.&nbsp;

00:07:35.280 --> 00:07:40.240
It wasn't easy to navigate, following the&nbsp;
directions of a child. What exactly did she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:40.240 --> 00:07:46.640
mean by "go past the rock shaped like a butt,"&nbsp;
or "look out for those purple flowers I like?"&nbsp;

00:07:46.640 --> 00:07:50.320
In spite of their obstacles, though,&nbsp;
they were able to get their bearings.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:50.320 --> 00:07:55.440
They realized they were getting close, though&nbsp;
close to what they couldn't quite be sure,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:55.440 --> 00:08:00.080
when Officer Rita Flinn stepped on something&nbsp;
that crunched loudly beneath her boot.&nbsp;

00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:04.480
"What the..." She lifted her shoe, to find&nbsp;
a piece of bright blue hard candy broken&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:04.480 --> 00:08:10.160
beneath the sole. Candy, in the middle of the&nbsp;
woods. As they searched the area around them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.160 --> 00:08:15.600
the rest of the officers found pieces of the&nbsp;
same candy, in different shapes and colors,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.600 --> 00:08:20.480
all strangely inviting for candy that they&nbsp;
found on the ground. They couldn't explain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:20.480 --> 00:08:25.200
the significance of the candy, but they&nbsp;
knew it meant they were getting close.&nbsp;

00:08:25.200 --> 00:08:29.360
They followed the multicolored candy trail, like&nbsp;
Hansel and Gretel tracking their path through&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:29.360 --> 00:08:34.480
the forest with crumbs of bread. They could&nbsp;
hear footsteps up ahead, coming from a nearby&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:34.480 --> 00:08:38.640
clearing. Through the trees, the team&nbsp;
of officers could make out a log cabin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.640 --> 00:08:43.680
that looked like it had been abandoned for quite&nbsp;
some time. As they drew closer to the cabin,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:43.680 --> 00:08:48.720
and the sounds of activity inside, several of&nbsp;
the officers suddenly froze in their tracks.&nbsp;

00:08:48.720 --> 00:08:53.680
They insisted they be allowed to turn back,&nbsp;
to go home. They couldn't explain why,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:53.680 --> 00:09:00.080
but they knew that they needed to leave, that&nbsp;
something did not want them there. Officer Flinn,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.080 --> 00:09:05.120
the only female officer in the group, scoffed at&nbsp;
her colleagues. She urged them not to be cowards,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:05.120 --> 00:09:11.120
and to keep moving. There were children's lives&nbsp;
at stake! This was no time to get cold feet.&nbsp;

00:09:11.120 --> 00:09:15.600
Still tentative, but feeling thoroughly shamed,&nbsp;
the rest of the officers followed Rita toward&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:15.600 --> 00:09:22.320
the cabin. So far, so good. No sign of the missing&nbsp;
boys, but no sign of foul play yet either. Then,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:22.320 --> 00:09:27.360
behind her, Flinn heard Officer Simon let&nbsp;
out a groan of pain. She turned and saw him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:27.360 --> 00:09:32.480
doubled over, clutching his stomach. Before&nbsp;
anyone could intervene, his knees buckled,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:32.480 --> 00:09:37.280
and he fell to the ground, suddenly&nbsp;
unconscious. Flinn ran to check his pulse,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:37.280 --> 00:09:42.560
and it was steady, but he wouldn't wake up.
His breath gave off a slightly sweet smell,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:42.560 --> 00:09:48.000
and she remembered her great uncle, and a trip&nbsp;
he'd taken to the hospital. Somehow, Officer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:48.000 --> 00:09:54.320
Simon had fallen into a diabetic coma, right there&nbsp;
in the woods. Before she had time to think too&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:54.320 --> 00:10:00.080
hard about it, Officer Paul collapsed in the exact&nbsp;
same way, right before her eyes. All around her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:00.080 --> 00:10:05.280
as they attempted to approach the cabin, Flinn's&nbsp;
fellow officers were dropping like flies.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:05.280 --> 00:10:11.360
She turned back to the cabin, and her eyes caught&nbsp;
a shock of pink hair as a woman stepped out. She&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:11.360 --> 00:10:17.360
made eye contact with Flinn, who took note of&nbsp;
her unusual, vivid pink eyes, and she waved.&nbsp;

00:10:17.360 --> 00:10:21.680
"Hi, there! What's your name?" She&nbsp;
called in a syrupy sweet voice.&nbsp;

00:10:21.680 --> 00:10:24.640
Officer Flinn drew her weapon.&nbsp;
"Hands where I can see them!"&nbsp;

00:10:24.640 --> 00:10:28.240
The pink-haired woman cocked her&nbsp;
head in confusion but complied.&nbsp;

00:10:28.240 --> 00:10:32.480
"No need to be so mean!" She&nbsp;
pouted. "It's just us girls!"&nbsp;

00:10:32.480 --> 00:10:37.600
But that wasn't entirely true. In the forest&nbsp;
behind the cabin, Officer Flinn could see&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:37.600 --> 00:10:43.600
humanoid figures, trudging through the trees.&nbsp;
But they weren't human, they were shiny, hard,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:43.600 --> 00:10:49.280
and brightly colored. She thought of the candy&nbsp;
she stepped on earlier, and her jaw dropped. As&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:49.280 --> 00:10:54.320
the candy people approached her, she began&nbsp;
to recognize their faces. The missing boys,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:54.320 --> 00:11:00.880
each and every one of them, transformed somehow&nbsp;
into living hard candy. Holding her weapon in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:00.880 --> 00:11:05.920
one hand, and keeping an eye on the pink-haired&nbsp;
woman and her tiny candy army all the while,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:05.920 --> 00:11:10.720
she pulled out her radio and called in&nbsp;
the strangest report she had ever made.&nbsp;

00:11:10.720 --> 00:11:16.240
No one in the town, not even the chief of&nbsp;
police, had ever heard of anything like this.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:16.240 --> 00:11:21.600
But fortunately, the police chief knew someone&nbsp;
who did. An old friend who devoted her time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:21.600 --> 00:11:27.440
to investigating cases that were impossible to&nbsp;
explain. Less than 24 hours after Officer Flinn&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:27.440 --> 00:11:33.680
made her call, the SCP Foundation was arriving&nbsp;
at the scene to collect the candy children, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:33.680 --> 00:11:40.160
the woman who would become known as Ms. Sweetie.
Officer Flinn's report, along with an in-depth&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:40.160 --> 00:11:45.600
study of both the hard candy pieces, and the hard&nbsp;
candy humanoids obtained from the crime scene,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:45.600 --> 00:11:50.880
offered some insight into Ms. Sweetie's abilities.&nbsp;
Her presence inherently repels men that come&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:50.880 --> 00:11:56.640
within 50 yards of her, and any man that enters&nbsp;
her radius will feel an immense desire to leave,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:56.640 --> 00:12:01.520
and go back in the opposite direction.
If he is forced to continue his approach,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:01.520 --> 00:12:06.080
then he will begin to feel ill,&nbsp;
experiencing nausea, shortness of breath,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:06.080 --> 00:12:11.920
and severe stomach pain. Finally, he will fall&nbsp;
into what resembles a spontaneous diabetic coma.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:11.920 --> 00:12:17.520
The only way for him to regain consciousness is&nbsp;
to be brought back outside of the 50-yard radius.&nbsp;

00:12:17.520 --> 00:12:22.320
As for the hard candy, Foundation researchers&nbsp;
gave one piece to a female D-Class,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:22.320 --> 00:12:27.520
and another piece to a male D-class, to test&nbsp;
the effect it might have on different genders.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:27.520 --> 00:12:32.000
When the woman ate her piece, she simply chewed,&nbsp;
swallowed, and looked at the attending researcher&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:32.000 --> 00:12:37.120
in confusion, as if to say, "Was that it?"
When the man ate his piece, however,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:37.120 --> 00:12:43.040
his body began to undergo a rapid transformation.&nbsp;
His blood sugar levels skyrocketed, rendering him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:43.040 --> 00:12:49.440
immobile almost immediately. Over the next twelve&nbsp;
hours, his flesh, bones, musculature, and all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:49.440 --> 00:12:55.280
other parts of his body began to crystallize into&nbsp;
hard candy. When the transformation was complete,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:55.280 --> 00:13:00.560
the new entity attempted to free Ms. Sweetie&nbsp;
from her containment. He was neutralized using&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:00.560 --> 00:13:05.440
a flamethrower, which melted the sugar&nbsp;
of his body down into a sticky puddle.&nbsp;

00:13:05.440 --> 00:13:09.840
Any person identifying as a male who eats&nbsp;
a piece of this hard candy will experience&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:09.840 --> 00:13:14.800
a similar effect, just as the missing&nbsp;
boys did. In some, very rare cases,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:14.800 --> 00:13:20.080
the transformed party will turn into a candy&nbsp;
unicorn, rather than a humanoid creature,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:20.080 --> 00:13:25.520
but the cause of these special cases is unknown.
After Ms. Sweetie was brought into Foundation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:25.520 --> 00:13:31.920
custody, and given her official designation of&nbsp;
SCP-2396, specialized containment procedures&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:31.920 --> 00:13:38.000
were put in place to keep her in captivity.&nbsp;
She was placed in Provisional Site 2396, and,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:38.000 --> 00:13:44.480
due to her distaste for men and boys, assigned a&nbsp;
research staff that consisted entirely of women.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:44.480 --> 00:13:50.160
Any men or masculine-identifying individuals&nbsp;
located within a 6 km radius of the site were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:50.160 --> 00:13:57.040
to be temporarily detained and questioned&nbsp;
about any possible contact with SCP-2396.&nbsp;

00:13:57.040 --> 00:14:02.960
So every night in Provisional Site 2396 was&nbsp;
Ladies' Night! But it wasn't much of a party.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:02.960 --> 00:14:09.680
Researchers were preoccupied with finding a way&nbsp;
to neutralize SCP-2396's anomalous effects. Most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:09.680 --> 00:14:16.960
notably, in spite of her containment, small pieces&nbsp;
of assorted hard candy - or SCP-2396-A - would be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:16.960 --> 00:14:22.320
spontaneously generated within a 6-kilometer&nbsp;
radius of Ms. Sweetie. Any of these that were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:22.320 --> 00:14:27.280
spotted would be incinerated on sight, but the&nbsp;
Mobile Task Force in charge of supervising the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:27.280 --> 00:14:32.240
area was having trouble keeping up. Male civilians&nbsp;
were slipping through the cracks, eating the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:32.240 --> 00:14:40.720
candy, and transforming into candy humanoids, or&nbsp;
instances of SCP-2396-B, then storming the Site&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:40.720 --> 00:14:46.720
and attempting to free Ms. Sweetie from captivity.&nbsp;
It was becoming untenable to keep her contained.&nbsp;

00:14:46.720 --> 00:14:52.720
The generation of instances of SCP-2396-A was&nbsp;
directly connected to her regular consumption&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:52.720 --> 00:14:58.960
of sugar in all of its forms, which she&nbsp;
requested as rations. The amount did not matter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:58.960 --> 00:15:04.400
nor did the form it took. She merely required&nbsp;
something sweet once a day. Sometimes it was a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:04.400 --> 00:15:09.440
bowl of pure cane sugar, sometimes a cup of&nbsp;
maple syrup. On a staff member's birthday,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:09.440 --> 00:15:14.000
they brought her a piece of chocolate cake,&nbsp;
which she was especially delighted by.&nbsp;

00:15:14.000 --> 00:15:19.040
Eventually, they settled on a single liter of&nbsp;
glucose syrup once a day, hoping it could slow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:19.040 --> 00:15:24.960
things down by eliminating any whimsy or variation&nbsp;
from the feedings. Every time, without fail,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:24.960 --> 00:15:31.680
more instances of the anomalous candy would&nbsp;
manifest soon after SCP-2396 ate her meal.&nbsp;

00:15:31.680 --> 00:15:35.760
There was talk of starving her, to see if&nbsp;
this could mitigate the generation of candies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:35.760 --> 00:15:41.840
but when denied sugary foods, Ms. Sweetie would&nbsp;
double over in pain, wailing about the agony she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:41.840 --> 00:15:46.000
felt. The head researcher at the Provisional&nbsp;
Site was horrified by the notion of torturing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:46.000 --> 00:15:51.920
an anomaly that had done no intentional harm&nbsp;
to anyone, and insisted they find another way.&nbsp;

00:15:51.920 --> 00:15:57.680
One researcher, Dr. O'Herlihy, proposed a&nbsp;
solution: why not try a sugar substitute?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:57.680 --> 00:16:04.240
They decided to test it out, giving SCP-2396&nbsp;
a liter of liquid sucralose, while behaving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:04.240 --> 00:16:09.200
as though it was her ordinary dose of sugar. She&nbsp;
accepted it graciously and made no complaints of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:09.200 --> 00:16:14.640
pain at all. After switching to the sucralose,&nbsp;
the candy stopped appearing. Ms. Sweetie was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:14.640 --> 00:16:20.640
reclassified as Euclid, and moved to Site-19.
After a week of the sucralose-based containment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:20.640 --> 00:16:27.040
procedures, Dr. O'Herlihy conducted her fifth&nbsp;
interview with SCP-2396. For the sake of avoiding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:27.040 --> 00:16:32.080
any potential outbursts, Ms. Sweetie was led&nbsp;
to believe that she was still producing candy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:32.080 --> 00:16:38.400
as well as living candy creatures. A transcript&nbsp;
of this interview is included in SCP-2396's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:38.400 --> 00:16:43.120
official file. Dr. O'Herlihy sat down at&nbsp;
the table, where Ms. Sweetie was already&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:43.120 --> 00:16:49.680
waiting with a pleasant smile on her face.
"Good morning, SCP-2396." Dr. O'Herlihy began.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:49.680 --> 00:16:53.760
Ms. Sweetie scoffed and giggled at this opener.
"Oh, come on, Cindy! You don't have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:53.760 --> 00:16:58.640
to be all stuffy with your best gal!"
Dr. O'Herlihy responded with a polite smile,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:58.640 --> 00:17:05.280
neglecting to correct SCP-2396 on the fact&nbsp;
that Cindy was not, in fact, her first name.&nbsp;

00:17:05.280 --> 00:17:12.480
"Alright, SCP-2396, are you aware another&nbsp;
SCP-2396-B attempted to breach your containment?"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:12.480 --> 00:17:15.920
She referred, here, to one of&nbsp;
Ms. Sweetie's candy soldiers.&nbsp;

00:17:15.920 --> 00:17:20.960
Ms. Sweetie giggled. "That's just boys. Always&nbsp;
gotta be makin' a big stink of things when they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:20.960 --> 00:17:26.800
wanna get your attention. Ain't it always like&nbsp;
that? Never a man, always a boy. Always beatin'&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:26.800 --> 00:17:31.200
up their friends when they think they're gettin'&nbsp;
too close. A man's always gotta have his hands&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:31.200 --> 00:17:35.440
busy or else they're gonna be in the air."
Dr. O'Herlihy pressed the matter, "They&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:35.440 --> 00:17:41.440
seem to be concentrating on taking you away&nbsp;
from here. Are you unhappy here, SCP-2396?"&nbsp;

00:17:41.440 --> 00:17:45.920
Ms. Sweetie sighed. "A woman ain't happy&nbsp;
anywhere. Isn't that what they say?"&nbsp;

00:17:45.920 --> 00:17:49.360
Dr. O'Herlihy frowned. "I am&nbsp;
not aware of any such saying."&nbsp;

00:17:49.360 --> 00:17:54.400
Ms. Sweetie shrugged. "It should be one. I&nbsp;
don't know, Lucy, I think it's just because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:54.400 --> 00:17:59.760
every gal wants a big strong lug to sweep&nbsp;
her off her feet, and these are sweet boys,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:59.760 --> 00:18:05.840
deep down. Even if they're sticky. I'm sure they'd&nbsp;
sweep you off your feet, too, if you girls asked."&nbsp;

00:18:05.840 --> 00:18:10.560
Dr. O'Herlihy thought about commenting on&nbsp;
the inherent sexism and heternormativity of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:10.560 --> 00:18:15.760
this statement, but thought better of it. She also&nbsp;
considered pointing out that Lucy was not her name&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:15.760 --> 00:18:18.480
either, but shook it off.
"Then what about the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:18.480 --> 00:18:23.200
instances that resemble unicorns?"
Ms. Sweetie lit up at the mention of these.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:23.200 --> 00:18:28.320
"Don't you just love unicorns? All little&nbsp;
girls love unicorns. You can eat them, too,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:28.320 --> 00:18:32.880
when you get bored. Little girls get bored.&nbsp;
It's good to have boys and unicorns you can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:32.880 --> 00:18:35.200
eat when you're finished."
"Isn't that a little&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:35.200 --> 00:18:40.240
reductive?" Dr. O'Herlihy replied.
Ms. Sweetie appeared to become irritated. She&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:40.240 --> 00:18:46.640
rolled her eyes. "Look, toots. I'm a girls' toy,&nbsp;
and it's a man's world. What do you want from me?"&nbsp;

00:18:46.640 --> 00:18:50.400
"Is that why you repel men?&nbsp;
Because you're a girls' toy?"&nbsp;

00:18:50.400 --> 00:18:55.200
Ms. Sweetie nodded. "Dr. W didn't like&nbsp;
it when boys break their sisters' toys.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:55.200 --> 00:18:59.840
Told me it was damn near the worst thing&nbsp;
in the world. And they can't break me.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:59.840 --> 00:19:04.960
They can't even come near me. Well, 'cept if&nbsp;
they're, you know, all sweet and handsome."&nbsp;

00:19:04.960 --> 00:19:09.200
"And you're happy with the way&nbsp;
things are?" Dr. O'Herlihy asked.&nbsp;

00:19:09.200 --> 00:19:13.760
Ms. Sweetie paused for a moment to consider,&nbsp;
then answered, "Dr. W's good in my book. I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:13.760 --> 00:19:18.960
always had a sweet tooth, and I always wanted to&nbsp;
be a girl. Kind of an okay trade-off, if you ask&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:18.960 --> 00:19:24.320
me. You guys ain't so bad, though. Even if the&nbsp;
food's crap. Don't know how you mess up sugar,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:24.320 --> 00:19:29.120
Sarah, but you guys make it taste like crap."
Aside from complaining about its taste, and no&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:29.120 --> 00:19:34.320
longer being able to produce any of her anomalous&nbsp;
candy, the sucralose substitute has had no adverse&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:34.320 --> 00:19:41.600
effects on SCP-2396. At this point in time, no&nbsp;
containment measures beyond this dietary change,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:41.600 --> 00:19:46.880
and making sure all staff that interact with&nbsp;
her identify as women, have been necessary.&nbsp;

00:19:46.880 --> 00:19:51.360
So, Ms. Sweetie sits in her cell in&nbsp;
the low-security wing of Site-19,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:51.360 --> 00:19:56.960
missing her favorite sugary treats, but otherwise&nbsp;
content with the way things are. And on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:56.960 --> 00:20:03.200
outside, no more unsuspecting boys are being&nbsp;
transformed into confectionary against their will.&nbsp;

00:20:03.200 --> 00:20:06.160
Just to be safe, though, if&nbsp;
you're ever out walking and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:06.160 --> 00:20:10.400
you see pieces of delicious-looking&nbsp;
hard candy scattered along the ground,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:10.400 --> 00:20:15.280
just remember what your parents always&nbsp;
said: Don't take candy from strangers.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:15.280 --> 00:20:21.920
You just never know where it came from.
Now go check out "SCP-001 - A Simple Toymaker"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:23.680 --> 00:20:29.520
and "ALL the Little Misters Explained" for more&nbsp;
on the mysterious creations of Dr. Wondertainment!

